<title>USA: Fed seen adding reserves at intervention period.</title>
<headline>Fed seen adding reserves at intervention period.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Reserve was expected to add resereves to the banking system on Monday at its usual intervention period either through term repurchase agreements (RPs) or overnight system RPs, economists said.</p>
<p>Fed funds were trading at 5.69 percent, higher than the Fed's current official target level of 5-1/2 percent.</p>
<p>(( -- North American Treasury Desk 212-859-1660))</p>
